2026-10-13: Transport framing, ownership and scatter/gather follow-up

- The matched GENERIC-NODEBUG kernel and module build passed (buildkernel.log),
  as did the refreshed build after probe-batch rollback (buildkernel-final.log).
- Failed virtual-probe batches now discard probes created by that batch and
  release empty provider reservations, preserving pre-existing probes.
- bhyve transport resets rotate receive-session generations and reconnect both
  channels. Delayed frames from the prior transport session are discarded.
  This does not solve reuse of kernel VM namespace IDs across VM destruction.
- libdtrace initializes ELF headers, sends complete bounded frames and consumes
  ACK/NAK under one framing lock. Async jobs own a duplicate socket and copied
  program identifier, so callers may destroy their program and close their
  socket after enqueueing. Queue admission, teardown and restart are bounded.
- The CLI ELF receiver checks complete frames and unaligned VM envelopes. Its
  VM-listing receiver now handles partial reads/EOF with an absolute deadline,
  bounds allocation counts, validates terminated names and accepts empty lists.
  The fixed-size listing deduplication array is replaced by sized storage.
- Guest control buffers may span two physical segments. bhyve gathers/scatters
  bounded descriptor chains and checks the complete capacity before copying.
  This removes the single-segment assertion and premature partial-copy risk.

