2026-10-13: Reset failure isolation, cancelable startup and PAE translation

- Backend frame publication is serialized through a generation check. An old
  frame's allocation/validation failure no longer poisons the freshly reset
  device. Old messages are discarded; current-session transport failures set
  NEEDS_RESET. Idle and not-yet-connected transports remain normal conditions.
- A failed/stopping device no longer emits READY acknowledgements. Guest ELF
  magic is checked before a completed program is forwarded to the host daemon.
- Guest daemon socket readiness waits now observe shutdown and have a ten-second
  deadline. Semaphore initialization errors are checked before launching threads.
- Probe-context address translation supports PAE roots at 32-byte boundaries,
  including roots at the end of a page, 4 KiB and 2 MiB mappings. It remains
  read-only and rejects invalid/reserved roots and addresses above 32 bits.
  This is page-walker support, not full 32-bit guest qualification; non-PAE
  translation and user-mode guest access remain unsupported.

