2026-10-13: Legacy translation, daemon process/spool ownership and ELF boundaries

- Added read-only non-PAE 32-bit page walks (4 KiB/4 MiB); reject addresses
  above 32 bits and PSE-36/reserved extended large-page bits. This supersedes
  the preceding note that non-PAE translation is unsupported. Guest user-mode
  access and full 32-bit guest qualification remain open.
- Removed 67-million-bucket preallocations from each daemon directory set.
  Directory state/empty-directory results are initialized; descriptors are
  CLOEXEC and paths normalized. Spool publication uses bounded streaming,
  complete I/O, hidden exclusive files, fsync/close and atomic rename, with
  failure cleanup. This does not claim rename durability across a host crash.
- Inbound/base launches use posix_spawn and parent-prepared arguments. Owned
  descriptors/children unwind on errors; malformed, unknown, truncated and
  failed identifier replies cannot leave an unmanaged child. The identifier
  exchange has a ten-second deadline. No-identifier guest stdio uses /dev/null.
- CLI identifier reads handle fragmented input, EOF, overflow, bounded sizes
  and deadlines. Daemon frame allocation failures now fail the request cleanly.
- ELF reader validates record bounds/alignment, array sizes, NUL-terminated
  strings and referenced DIFO table lengths; bounds recursive format chains
  and rejects cyclic statement/action chains. Statement/options failures are
  propagated. Enabled-probe counts cannot exceed the containing section.
- Checksummed ELF input requires a bounded regular file with a complete header
  and body. Temporary descriptors are parser-owned; temporary files are unlinked
  before parsing. Full reads/writes and corrected checksum diagnostic formatting
  replace unchecked short I/O. Success acknowledgement follows complete parsing.
- The ELF translation unit enables exceptions and catches std::bad_alloc at
  its C entry points. Parsed printf descriptors own prefix bytes in their own
  allocation, matching the existing printf destructor; partial format objects
  unwind on failure. Several explicit allocation-failure aborts were removed.
  This is not a claim that every parser allocation/error path has been audited.

