Measured memory cost: baseline FreeBSD mbuf is 256 bytes with 64-byte packet
header. The imported packet ID raises the packet header to 96 bytes and
sizeof(struct mbuf) to 288; the branch currently uses MSIZE=512. This overhead
requires an explicit representation/ABI design and performance qualification,
not a blind size reset. Snapshot/external-session replay, network provenance,
remaining daemon failure paths and live qualification are still open. No
installation, module load, guest launch, upgrade or reboot was performed.

2026-10-13: daemon failure-path continuation

- buildworld-accept-oom.log completed successfully at 18:58:25 UTC. It
  preceded the final directory/dispatch changes below.
- Partial daemon thread creation now requests shutdown and joins only threads
  that actually started. The semaphore is destroyed only if initialized.
  Partial thread creation has not yet been fault-injected end to end.
- READ_DATA dispatch catches allocation failure and releases the new job.
  WRITE dispatch splices its existing queue node, requiring no new allocation.
  Socket retirement retains ownership in the live socket set and requests
  shutdown if the dead-socket set cannot allocate a node.
- Directory construction reports system errors instead of aborting. Startup
  owns partial directories with scoped pointers, closes the transport and
  bound socket on failure, and keeps the original error code. Finalization
  closes the transport even when socket removal reports an error.
- Directory scans now detect readdir errors. NOTIFY_ELFWRITE jobs are prepared
  as a batch, including path copies and list nodes, before the file is marked
  seen. The whole batch is then spliced into the work queue without further
  allocation. Failure before commit drops every prepared job and reference.
