2026-10-13: daemon transport connection continuation

The local forwarder uses a nonblocking Unix socket. Its connect path now
waits for POLLOUT and checks SO_ERROR through an absolute deadline, accepting
EINPROGRESS/EALREADY/EINTR as pending states. The same two-second deadline
covers connection completion and the initial two handshake transfers. A
failed or timed-out connect closes the socket instead of leaving a half-open
forwarder. native-daemon-round36.log passes thirteen sanitized suites,
including a real local nonblocking connection and injected pending, refusal,
SO_ERROR and timeout outcomes. buildworld-connect-final.log completed at
19:18:03 UTC. It compiled dtraced_job.cc just before the worker fix below,
so it is not the final build for this source. No live daemon or guest was
started.

2026-10-13: daemon worker failure continuation

Sending a client-info snapshot now catches allocation failure and reports
ENOMEM to the worker instead of letting an exception terminate its thread.
ELF and cleanup debug messages no longer construct temporary C++ strings;
two cleanup error formats now match their string arguments. The injected
allocation test verifies that an info-send failure sends no partial frame,
keeps its client reference balanced, and permits a later successful send.
